  "title": "AJILE12: long-term naturalistic ECoG with wrist-movement events and behaviour labels (DANDI 000055)",
  "description": "AJILE12 provides long-term, naturalistic electrocorticography (ECoG) recorded opportunistically from 12 participants during clinical epilepsy monitoring at Harborview Medical Center, totaling 55 recording days (about 1295 h). The recordings are accompanied by wrist-movement initiation events and coarse behavioural state labels derived from simultaneous video. This iEEG-BIDS representation converts the original NWB release from DANDI 000055 without changing signal values. No experimental task was performed.",
  "methods_description": "ECoG (grids, strips and some depth electrodes) was recorded passively at 1 kHz during 24-hour clinical monitoring, with simultaneous 30 fps video. The authors processed the data with median DC removal, 1-200 Hz band-pass, 60 Hz notch, downsampling to 500 Hz and common median re-referencing. Wrist-movement events were detected and visually validated from video-based pose estimation, and coarse behaviours were annotated. Electrodes were localised with FieldTrip and warped to MNI space.",
